\fs22
\b Replit AI Master Prompt for Brunei Finance App MVP\b0\par
\par
\f1 Copy the prompt below into Replit AI to begin scaffolding the app.\f0\par
\par
Build a full-stack web MVP called \b DuitPlan\b0 , a Brunei-first personal finance app for salaried users. Use \b Next.js with TypeScript\b0 , \b Tailwind CSS\b0 , \b shadcn/ui\b0 , \b Prisma\b0 , and \b PostgreSQL\b0 . Design it as a clean, modern, responsive dashboard app.\par
\par
\b Core product purpose\b0 : help Brunei users manage monthly salary, expenses, debt obligations, and bank statement imports from local banks.\par
\par
\b Build these MVP modules:\b0\par
1. Authentication\par
- email/password sign up and login\par
- protected app routes\par
\par
2. Onboarding\par
- collect full name\par
- monthly salary\par
- payday\par
- fixed commitments\par
- debts\par
- starter budget categories\par
\par
3. Dashboard\par
- total monthly income\par
- total commitments\par
- amount spent this month\par
- amount remaining\par
- debt summary\par
- top spending categories\par
- simple insights cards\par
\par
4. Transactions\par
- transactions list\par
- add/edit/delete transaction\par
- fields: date, amount, type, description, merchant, category, account, source, notes\par
- category filters and date filters\par
\par
5. Budgets\par
- monthly budget allocation by category\par
- compare planned vs actual\par
- show remaining budget\par
\par
6. Debts\par
- add/edit multiple debts\par
- fields: debt type, lender, outstanding balance, monthly payment, interest/profit rate optional\par
- simple payoff simulation with extra monthly payment input\par
\par
7. Statement Import\par
- upload PDF statement\par
- support BIBD and Baiduri as initial bank types\par
- create a modular parser architecture with one parser per bank\par
- for now, parser can use mock parser logic with structured placeholders if real parsing is not complete\par
- show review table before saving imported transactions\par
- allow user to edit categories before confirming import\par
\par
8. Insights\par
- generate rules-based insights such as top spending category, debt-to-income ratio, spending increase from previous month, and remaining amount before payday\par
\par
9. Settings\par
- profile settings\par
- payday and salary settings\par
- category management\par
\par
10. Premium placeholder\par
- create a premium page showing future paid features like statement import, debt payoff simulation, and advanced insights\par
\par
\b Data model requirements\b0\par
Create Prisma models for:\par
- User\par
- Profile\par
- Account\par
- Commitment\par
- Category\par
- Transaction\par
- MonthlyBudget\par
- Debt\par
- DebtScenario\par
- UploadedDocument\par
- ImportedTransactionRow\par
- MerchantRule\par
- Insight\par
- SubscriptionPlan\par
- UserSubscription\par
\par
\b UX requirements\b0\par
- make the app simple, calm, and modern\par
- use cards, summary blocks, tables, and guided forms\par
- avoid heavy accounting language\par
- make onboarding easy and step-by-step\par
- make dashboard the default home page after login\par
- optimize for trust and clarity\par
\par
\b Important constraints\b0\par
- do not build direct bank login integration\par
- do not auto-save imported transactions without review\par
- keep architecture clean and modular\par
- use mock parser logic if necessary, but structure code so real parser logic can be added later\par
\par
\b Deliverables expected from the scaffold\b0\par
- file/folder structure\par
- app router pages\par
- reusable UI components\par
- Prisma schema\par
- seed data for sample categories\par
- basic dashboard data wiring\par
- placeholder parser services for BIBD and Baiduri\par
- clean README with setup instructions\par
\par
Start by generating the project structure, Prisma schema, app routes, layout, and onboarding flow first. Then proceed module by module.\par
}